Hi Eric,

I'm sending the editable R03 manuscript, my separate response to Nicole's nin=
e final methods points, and a location table for your editorial check. Seven =
points are reflected in the manuscript. I have kept the July result out of Fi=
gure 1 because it uses a different evaluation set and comparator, and have no=
t distributed the internal cross-channel case correspondence table. The respo=
nse explains both decisions; Case Allocation gives the aggregate shared-case =
counts instead.

The table maps each numbered point to the R03 heading, including Figure 1, wi=
th a short marker to help you find the relevant change. The figure now shows =
both values and the common evaluation denominator directly; the abstract also=
 identifies the 160 as selected development errors.

Please let me know if anything in the editable files needs clarification for =
the next stage.

Best,
Vanessa

